Subject: [PATCH] propers(54): repair the displaced reader order that broke the
 deploy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Run 3c3fb16baa13ee6b, `author-proper` iteration 0. Seeded because the
49-commit fast-forward to origin/main carried this leaf's unfinished
production onto main, where the deploy typesets what it had been serving from
cache and the build stopped: `brief synthesis must begin on page 3, as the
profile fixes it, not page 4`.

The displacement was in **both** editions, not the companion alone. The
canonical `.aux` also carried `brief-synthesis:start` at page 4; the canonical
build target does not run the `--aux` gate, so it built while displaced and
only the companion failed. Cause: `1567fb53b`'s traditional-attribution
relation lengthened the generated Date cells, which this stage may not edit, so
the page-2 sheet spilled its Epistle dossier onto page 3. Repaired by
tightening the seven dossiers' explanatory prose without dropping a fact, and
by reinstating the sheet's three documented measurement departures in
`format.tex` with a note stating them and why. Both editions now build at 76
and 45 pages with start/end/next at 3/4/5.

The two standing blocking findings this leaf carried are repaired:

- `CON-CIT-110` — the Postcommunion's second `semper` paragraph. The brief's
  own denominator does take in the Fifteenth Sunday, so the clause claiming it
  did not was itself false. Re-swept over the collated records: `semper` stands
  in an appointed oration of four of the fifteen identities, twice in two of
  them, with two further identities carrying it in a chant -- the Fifth's
  Offertory and the Twelfth's Gradual, where the finding had said "Introit"
  and named no element for the Twelfth. The paragraph now agrees with
  `50-interpretive.tex`.
- `CON-CIT-107` — the nine named locators were already correct in the tree.
  The sweep its `required_result` demanded is now done: every `above`,
  `below`, `here`, `there` and "the commentary" locator in all eight shared
  files read and tested against the rebuilt companion, all resolving in both
  editions.

`notable-and-quotable` moves ahead of `exploratory-synthesis` into the
profile's reader order. The page-2 sheet's one verbatim encyclopedia
reproduction is now reported rather than reproduced. `research/scope.md`,
`synthesis.tex`, the edition guards and `sections/synthesis/` are untouched.

Verified before advancing, not taken on report: both editions build,
`check-proper-components --aux` on the companion exits 0 where it was the
command CI failed on, and all twelve `check-content-preflight` checks pass.

